% Beard Tax Act
%
% The Logical English twin of a Blawx encoding, written by the Blawx translator
% (InsurLE2/migration/blawx). Each rule is a rule of the Act as Blawx encodes it,
% in the words of Blawx's own sentence forms, citing its section; the project's
% tests are the scenarios, with Blawx's own answers as the expectations.
%
% Source: the Blawx project "Beard Tax Act" (beard_tax.yaml, 4 sections), an example of
%         Blawx v1.6.22-alpha (Lexpedite, MIT licence), commit 3de892f67854292b304c9a55c5e2cd2058d3d418.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* is bearded.
    *a person* is a person; scenario element.
    the facial hair of *a person* is *a number* mm in length; scenario element.
    *a person* qualifies under section 1 a.
    *a person* qualifies under section 1 b.
    the facial hair of *a person* is on the chin; scenario element.
    the facial hair of *a person* is below the chin; scenario element.
    the facial hair of *a person* is ear to ear below the nose; scenario element.

the knowledge base beard_tax includes:

the text of the Beard Tax Act is at "sources/beard_tax.md".

the text of the Blawx project is at "sources/beard_tax.yaml".

% The Act, section by section.
rule section_1 with provenance the Beard Tax Act at section 1:
a person is bearded if
    the person is a person
    and the facial hair of the person is a number N mm in length
    and N >= 5
    and the person qualifies under section 1 a.

rule section_1_2 with provenance the Beard Tax Act at section 1:
a person is bearded if
    the person is a person
    and the facial hair of the person is a number N mm in length
    and N >= 5
    and the person qualifies under section 1 b.

rule section_1_a with provenance the Beard Tax Act at section 1 a:
a person qualifies under section 1 a if
    the facial hair of the person is on the chin.

rule section_1_a_2 with provenance the Beard Tax Act at section 1 a:
a person qualifies under section 1 a if
    the facial hair of the person is below the chin.

rule section_1_b with provenance the Beard Tax Act at section 1 b:
a person qualifies under section 1 b if
    the facial hair of the person is ear to ear below the nose.

scenario are_they_bearded is, as stated in the Blawx project at test are_they_bearded:
    are_they_bearded expects answers [].

scenario case_1 is, as stated in the case analysis of the encoding at section 1:
    % a case of the rule of section 1 (blawx_cases.pl), answered by Blawx
    person_a is a person.
    the facial hair of person_a is 5 mm in length.
    person_a qualifies under section 1 a.
    which_is_bearded expects answers ["person_a is bearded"].

